    ],
    "synthesis_summary": "The temporal trajectory traces a clear intellectual sequence across 250 years: from classical approximation and equilibrium (1750–1917) to dynamical vector-field stability (1892–1945), culminating in the Cold War twin pinnacles of admissible optimal control (Pontryagin, Krasovskii) and ill-posed inverse regularization (Tikhonov, Gelfand-Levitan). The overarching grammatical evolution demonstrates that the Soviet mathematical style is not static dogma but an expanding operator calculus adapting continuously from Imperial mechanics to Cold War technology."
